00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.570
I should probably clarify that there are some writers who work in teaMs.
我应该说明一下，有些编剧是以团队形式工作的。

197
00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:45.390
Yes.
是的。

198
00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.730
Like we've mentioned before, Gene and Lee.
就像我们之前提到的，吉恩和李。

199
00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.190
They were a writing team.
他们是一个编剧搭档。

200
00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:51.210
They were hired together as a duo.
他们是作为二人组一起被雇佣的。

201
00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.410
But Justin and Brent were not a writing team.
但贾斯汀和布伦特并不是一个编剧搭档。

202
00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.130
They were hired separately.
他们是分别被聘用的。

203
00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:00.090
So this was interesting that they were co-writing this together.
所以他们能一起合写这一集很有意思。

204
00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:05.230
Well, we reached out to both of them to hear what it was like to be paired together on this
我们联系了他们两人，想听听他们对这次搭档合作的感受，

205
00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:05.630
episode.
关于这一集。

206
00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:10.170
So they said that Greg just paired them together because he thought it would be kind of fun.
他们说，格雷格之所以把他们凑在一起，纯粹是因为觉得这样会很有趣。

207
00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.950
And Justin told me that they basically just split it down the middle, that Brent took a
贾斯汀告诉我，他们基本上是平分了工作，布伦特先写了

208
00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:15.930
pass at act one.
第一幕。

209
00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.550
Justin did act two.
贾斯汀写了第二幕。

210
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.110
And then they split act three.
然后他们分担了第三幕。

211
00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:22.950
And then they came together one afternoon and they kind of went over it.
之后他们找了个下午聚在一起，把内容过了一遍。

212
00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:29.310
And since Brent was the senior writer, he kind of took the lead on a kind of a dual rewrite.
由于布伦特是资深编剧，他主要负责了后续的联合修改工作。

213
00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:34.710
And then they turned it in and it was kind of, you know, punched up by the staff like every other
接着他们提交了剧本，就像其他剧集一样，由制作组进行了

214
00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:35.190
episode.
润色。

215
00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:40.310
I could see Greg doing this because he loved pairing together people to see what would come
我能理解格雷格为什么这么做，因为他喜欢把人凑在一起，看看这种组合会产生

216
00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.910
out of that pairing, whether it was characters or writers.
什么样的火花，无论是角色还是编剧。

217
00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:45.110
You know, he loved to see what happened.
你知道，他喜欢观察会发生什么。

218
00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:47.970
Even our editors sometimes were paired up in different ways.
甚至我们的剪辑师有时也会以不同的方式进行搭档。

219
00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:55.090
Well, Brent said that it's true that Greg did make it clear that he was the senior writer and
布伦特说，格雷格确实明确过他是资深编剧，

220
00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.010
that he had final decision on what went into the draft.
并且对最终定稿拥有决定权。

221
00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.830
But he said right from the start, he could see that Justin's scenes were just so good
但他表示，从一开始他就看出贾斯汀写的场景太棒了，

222
00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:08.150
that it would be a terrible mistake to put, quote, my grubby fingers on any of it, end quote.
如果去动它简直是犯傻，用他的话说就是“别让我的脏手去碰任何东西”。

223
00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:14.030
So he said that they didn't change any of each other's work.
所以他说他们没有改动对方的任何作品。

224
00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.570
They ended up turning it in just as they had both originally written it.
最终他们提交的剧本和他们最初写的一模一样。

225
00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.210
Well, that is so fun.
哇，那太有趣了。

226
00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:19.810
All right.
好的。

227
00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:26.310
Fast fact number two, I asked these guys, what was the inspiration for this episode?
第二个快讯，我问了他们，这一集的灵感来源是什么？

228
00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.070
Was this based on anything in real life?
它是基于现实生活中的什么事情吗？

229
00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:34.750
And Justin told me that he couldn't remember exactly where the idea came from, but he's pretty
贾斯汀告诉我，他不记得这个点子具体是怎么来的了，但他很确定

230
00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.230
sure that it just came out of one of those pitch sessions in the room.
它就是出自编剧室的头脑风暴会议。

231
00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:43.390
So it wasn't like one writer had the idea, but it was sort of a collective, one of your
所以并不是某个编剧单独想到的，而是一种集体创作，

232
00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:44.930
group mind things, Ange.
一种集体智慧的产物，安吉。

233
00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.810
Oh, I like group mind.
哦，我喜欢“集体智慧”这个说法。

234
00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:51.910
Well, he said he does have a very distinct memory as they were circling closer and closer
他说他有一个非常清晰的记忆，当时他们正越来越接近

235
00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:53.550
to something that felt like an episode.
一个成型的剧集构思。

236
00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:57.590
Lee Eisenberg suddenly blurted out, a product recall.
李·艾森伯格突然脱口而出：产品召回。

237
00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.070
It's a product recall.
就是产品召回。

238
00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:05.550
And after Lee said that, they knew it was going to be like a defective product and a mini
李说完之后，他们就知道这会是一个关于缺陷产品和小型

239
00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:06.010
scandal.
丑闻的故事。

240
00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.070
But here's the thing, Ange.
但重点来了，安吉。

241
00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.590
Here is why I asked.
这就是我为什么要问的原因。

242
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.870
I did a little Googling.
我稍微搜了一下。

243
00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:14.530
This episode aired in April 2007.
这一集是在2007年4月播出的。

244
00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:23.570
And the crazy thing is that in August of 2007, there was a massive, historic Mattel toy recall.
疯狂的是，在2007年8月，美泰公司发生了一次大规模、史无前例的玩具召回事件。

245
00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.390
A huge product recall.
一次巨大的产品召回。

246
00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:27.730
What did they recall?
他们召回了什么？

247
00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.550
They recalled 19 million toys.
他们召回了1900万件玩具。

248
00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:31.970
What was it?
是什么玩具？

249
00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:35.530
Some of them were recalled because they had lead paint.
其中一些被召回是因为含有铅漆。

250
00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.330
Was it a GI Joe?
是特种部队玩偶吗？

251
00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.790
No, I don't know what it was.
不，我不知道那是什么。

252
00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:41.450
A bunch of toys that were shown to have lead paint.
是一堆被查出含有铅漆的玩具。

253
00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:46.390
And the other was because there was a tiny magnet that kept falling off and it posed a choking
另一个原因是有一个小磁铁总是掉下来，造成了窒息

254
00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:46.830
hazard.
危险。

255
00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:52.550
But also in 2007, there was a massive crib recall.
但同样是在2007年，发生了一次大规模的婴儿床召回事件。

256
00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.650
One million Graco and Simplicity cribs were recalled.
一百万张Graco和Simplicity品牌的婴儿床被召回。

257
00:11:56.890 --> 00:12:03.990
And I even read an article that called 2007, quote, the year of the recall.
我甚至读到过一篇文章，称2007年为“召回之年”。

258
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.970
Well, that's crazy.
天哪，这太疯狂了。

259
00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.810
I wonder if it was in the zeitgeiSt.
我在想这是否是一种时代精神。

260
00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.470
It was in the group mind of the world.
那是全球集体潜意识的一部分。

261
00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:15.110
And it went into Lee's brain and he shouted it into the writer's room.
它进入了李的大脑，然后他把它喊进了编剧室。

262
00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:15.690
Yeah.
没错。

263
00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.410
And it became an episode of The Office.
然后它就成了《办公室》的一集内容。

264
00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:18.870
Major group mind.
重大的集体潜意识。

265
00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.370
That's some global group mind.
那真是某种全球性的集体潜意识。

266
00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.290
Okay, lady.
好吧，女士。

267
00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.450
I'm going to move us along to fast fact number three.
我要带大家进入第三个快速事实了。

268
00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.810
I'm calling it location alert.
我把它称为“地点警报”。

269
00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:27.130
Okay.
好的。

270
00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:33.070
As part of this episode, Jim and Andy go to a local high school to apologize for the obscene
在这一集中，吉姆和安迪去了一所当地的高中，为那个淫秽的

271
00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:33.830
watermark.
水印道歉。

272
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.710
And Kentopedia let us know because we got some mail.
肯托百科（Kentopedia）告诉了我们，因为我们收到了一些邮件。

273
00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.950
People wanted to know, was this the same school where we shot Diwali?
人们想知道，这和我们拍摄《排灯节》那一集是同一所学校吗？

274
00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.370
People love to know about locations.
人们很喜欢了解拍摄地点。

275
00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:44.690
They love it.
他们非常喜欢。

276
00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.990
This was filmed at a different school than Diwali.
这次拍摄的学校和《排灯节》那次不一样。

277
00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:52.930
This time we filmed at St. John Paul Academy in Burbank.
这次我们是在伯班克的圣约翰保罗学院拍摄的。

278
00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:57.810
In real life, it is a private Catholic STEM immersion high school.
在现实生活中，这是一所私立的天主教STEM沉浸式高中。

279
00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:01.070
The school colors are white, blue, and red.
学校的校色是白色、蓝色和红色。

280
00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.390
And the real students at the school wear uniforMs.
学校里的真实学生都穿着制服。

281
00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.710
For our shoot, we hired background performers to play the students.
为了拍摄，我们雇佣了临时演员来扮演学生。

282
00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:11.150
We did not use the actual students of this school.
我们没有使用这所学校真正的学生。

283
00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:16.350
I feel like that is a thorough answer to this location question.
我觉得对于这个地点问题，这已经是一个非常详尽的回答了。

284
00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.150
Yeah.
没错。

285
00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.570
You know, I went to a Catholic high school.
你知道吗，我上的是一所天主教高中。

286
00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:20.490
I know this.
我知道这一点。

287
00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.530
It was not co-ed.
那不是男女同校的。

288
00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.350
It was all girls.
那是全女子学校。

289
00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.910
And I wore a uniform.
我当时也穿制服。

290
00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:29.430
And our colors were green and white and gray and navy.
我们的校色是绿色、白色、灰色和海军蓝。

291
00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.770
I think were the colors we were allowed to wear.
我想我们被允许穿的颜色就是这些。

292
00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:32.270
And yellow.
还有黄色。

293
00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:33.850
That's a lot of colors.
那颜色可真多。

294
00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.390
It's really only five.
其实只有五种而已。

295
00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.490
And you're only allowed to wear those colors.
而且你只被允许穿这些颜色。

296
00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:40.490
Seems like a lot.
感觉还是挺多的。

297
00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:41.690
Scale it back.
精简一下吧。

298
00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:43.750
Do you wear...
你穿的是……

299
00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:46.870
How many colors do you wear?
你平时穿几种颜色？

300
00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.450
I just grab whatever's, you know, there.
我就是随手抓起什么就穿什么，你知道的。

301
00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:51.850
Right.
没错。

302
00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:56.110
So imagine you're getting dressed in the morning and you have to limit it to only these five
想象一下你早上穿衣服时，必须把颜色限制在

303
00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:56.510
colors.
这五种以内。

304
00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:57.310
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

305
00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.690
A friend of mine did that thing.
我有个朋友就这么干过。

306
00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:02.150
Remember when ladies would get their colors done?
还记得以前女士们会去做色彩鉴定吗？

307
00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.390
Oh, yes.
哦，记得。

308
00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.290
And you find out if you're like fall or spring.
就是去测你是秋季型还是春季型。

309
00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.250
A summer or a winter or something.
夏季型、冬季型之类的。

310
00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.170
My mom did this.
我妈做过这个。

311
00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.330
My mom was a summer.
我妈是夏季型。

312
00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:10.170
Okay.
好吧。

313
00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.090
So a friend of mine recently did this.
