Unless I feel like that happened more back in the day, like on Bewitched.
除非我觉得这种情况在过去更常见，比如在《神仙俏女巫》里。

1257
00:57:41.100 --> 00:57:44.180
Weren't there two Darens and like it was never explained or something?
不是有两个达伦吗，而且好像从来没解释过还是怎么着？

1258
00:57:44.180 --> 00:57:46.680
Well, that's like a major character change.
嗯，那可是主要角色的变动。

1259
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:49.480
This is like a guest role, right?
这只是个客串角色，对吧？

1260
00:57:49.960 --> 00:57:53.300
But they hired the same actress in three different guest roles.
但他们雇了同一个女演员演了三个不同的客串角色。

1261
00:57:53.780 --> 00:57:54.760
They loved her.
他们很喜欢她。

1262
00:57:55.120 --> 00:57:55.560
Clearly.
显而易见。

1263
00:57:57.120 --> 00:57:57.560
Clearly.
很明显。

1264
00:57:57.720 --> 00:57:58.420
Well, I loved her.
嗯，我很喜欢她。

1265
00:57:58.500 --> 00:57:59.740
I thought she was great on our show.
我觉得她在我们节目里表现得很棒。

1266
00:57:59.960 --> 00:58:01.080
She was so good.
她真的太出色了。

1267
00:58:01.080 --> 00:58:05.040
And she really just, I mean, pushed Michael over the edge.
而且她真的，我是说，把迈克尔逼到了崩溃的边缘。

1268
00:58:05.220 --> 00:58:06.080
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1269
00:58:06.740 --> 00:58:10.600
You know, Jen, I did say what could have made this press conference worse.
你知道吗，简，我确实说过还有什么能让这场新闻发布会变得更糟。

1270
00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:13.000
And Dwight, once again, does not help.
而德怀特，又一次，一点忙都没帮上。

1271
00:58:14.180 --> 00:58:15.560
Both animals were smiling.
两只动物都在笑。

1272
00:58:16.460 --> 00:58:20.740
There is a fantastic Dwight talking head where he talks about growing up on a farm.
德怀特有一段精彩的单人采访，他在里面谈到了在农场长大的经历。

1273
00:58:20.740 --> 00:58:23.860
And he has seen a lot of animal action.
而且他见过很多动物交配的场景。

1274
00:58:24.140 --> 00:58:29.520
And he says really matter-of-factly, whoever drew this got it exactly right.
他非常客观地评价说，画这幅画的人画得一点都没错。

1275
00:58:29.840 --> 00:58:30.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1276
00:58:30.300 --> 00:58:36.600
He tries to tell Mrs. Allen that the cartoon did seem to depict a consensual sex act.
他试图告诉艾伦夫人，那幅漫画看起来确实描绘了一种双方自愿的性行为。

1277
00:58:37.440 --> 00:58:38.800
Because they were smiling.
因为他们当时在笑。

1278
00:58:39.100 --> 00:58:40.200
And Dwight would know.
而且德怀特肯定懂这个。

1279
00:58:40.500 --> 00:58:40.780
Right.
没错。

1280
00:58:41.020 --> 00:58:41.880
Because of his farm life.
因为他在农场长大。

1281
00:58:42.240 --> 00:58:42.580
Right.
没错。

1282
00:58:42.580 --> 00:58:45.160
Well, Michael is really upset.
好吧，迈克尔真的很心烦。

1283
00:58:45.320 --> 00:58:46.600
He starts to vent to Pam.
他开始向帕姆发泄。

1284
00:58:46.840 --> 00:58:48.680
I mean, that things got out of control.
我是说，事情已经失控了。

1285
00:58:48.680 --> 00:58:50.800
It's going to be a national story.
这会成为全国性新闻的。

1286
00:58:50.900 --> 00:58:53.200
She's like, Michael, this is the Scranton Times.
她说，迈克尔，这可是《斯克兰顿时报》啊。

1287
00:58:53.480 --> 00:58:54.420
And he's like, no.
而他说，不。

1288
00:58:54.740 --> 00:58:58.240
We need to do an apology video.
我们需要拍个道歉视频。

1289
00:58:58.440 --> 00:59:00.520
Well, then Michael pulls out the video camera.
于是迈克尔拿出了摄像机。

1290
00:59:00.620 --> 00:59:04.880
And Jenna, the look on your face as Pam is so brilliant.
珍娜，你作为帕姆时的表情真是太精彩了。

1291
00:59:05.180 --> 00:59:07.040
It's so brilliant, Jenna.
太精彩了，珍娜。

1292
00:59:07.040 --> 00:59:10.560
It said so much history.
那里面包含了太多的过往。

1293
00:59:10.980 --> 00:59:15.880
How many videos has Pam had to film of Michael apologizing for things?
帕姆到底被迫给迈克尔拍过多少次道歉视频了？

1294
00:59:16.060 --> 00:59:21.260
I will tell you in the deleted scenes, there's a runner of videos and they're fantastic.
我得告诉你，在删减片段里，有一系列这样的视频，它们简直太棒了。

1295
00:59:21.260 --> 00:59:30.420
I was going to say that, that we shot a whole bunch of former apology videos and they didn't make it in the episode.
我正想说这个，我们拍了一大堆以前的道歉视频，但没能放进正片里。

1296
00:59:31.420 --> 00:59:43.840
I will tell you that shooting this scene with Steve and Rain and then also these old apology videos is some of the most fun I ever had on the show.
我得说，和史蒂夫、雷恩一起拍这场戏，还有那些旧的道歉视频，是我在剧组里最开心的时光之一。

1297
00:59:44.280 --> 00:59:46.960
It was so hard to get through these.
拍这些的时候太难忍住不笑了。

1298
00:59:47.160 --> 00:59:48.160
It was so difficult.
真的太难了。

1299
00:59:48.640 --> 00:59:50.240
I don't know how you did it.
我不知道你是怎么做到的。

1300
00:59:50.380 --> 00:59:55.160
And everything about your expressions, Jenna, are perfection.
而且关于你的表情，珍娜，一切都堪称完美。

1301
00:59:55.720 --> 01:00:00.480
You don't give away much, but it says so much about what Pam is thinking.
你虽然没怎么流露表情，但那眼神已经道尽了帕姆的心思。

1302
01:00:01.100 --> 01:00:03.140
I just thought you did a phenomenal job.
我觉得你演得真是太棒了。

1303
01:00:03.140 --> 01:00:05.000
And I loved these scenes.
我特别喜欢这些片段。

1304
01:00:05.120 --> 01:00:06.760
I love seeing the deleted ones.
我喜欢看那些删减片段。

1305
01:00:06.940 --> 01:00:07.880
I want to see more.
我还想看更多。

1306
01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:12.340
I could just see a clip show of all these videos that you guys had to do.
我真想看一个集锦，把你们当时拍的所有这些视频都剪进去。

1307
01:00:12.340 --> 01:00:14.200
And I love the small touches.
而且我喜欢那些小细节。

1308
01:00:14.440 --> 01:00:19.460
I love the American flag behind him, clearly made out of four pieces of paper taped together.
我喜欢他身后的那面美国国旗，明显是用四张纸拼在一起贴出来的。

1309
01:00:19.740 --> 01:00:19.880
Yep.
没错。

1310
01:00:20.180 --> 01:00:30.860
And I loved that from 15 minutes, 55 seconds to 16 minutes, 5 seconds, Dwight is just spraying Michael's hair.
我特别喜欢从15分55秒到16分05秒那段，德怀特一直在给迈克尔喷发胶。

1311
01:00:31.160 --> 01:00:31.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1312
01:00:32.100 --> 01:00:39.590
11 seconds of silence except for while he sprays the hair.
除了喷发胶的声音，整整11秒鸦雀无声。

1313
01:00:40.070 --> 01:00:41.510
I couldn't get through that.
我当时都快憋不住了。

1314
01:00:41.890 --> 01:00:43.430
I laughed so hard.
我笑得不行。

1315
01:00:43.430 --> 01:00:44.810
I broke constantly.
我一直在笑场。

1316
01:00:44.810 --> 01:00:47.330
It was very, very difficult to get through that.
拍那段戏真的太难太难了。

1317
01:00:47.510 --> 01:00:52.930
When you think about the real estate of a show, like every little moment counts.
当你考虑到一部剧的篇幅时，每一个小瞬间都很重要。

1318
01:00:53.110 --> 01:00:55.850
You're trying to just jam it with as much as possible.
你总是想尽可能多地塞进一些内容。

1319
01:00:55.850 --> 01:00:59.150
And I loved that our show would take these beats like this.
我喜欢我们的剧会留出这样的节奏。

1320
01:00:59.510 --> 01:00:59.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1321
01:00:59.850 --> 01:01:00.290
11 seconds.
整整11秒。

1322
01:01:00.290 --> 01:01:01.430
No one's saying a word.
谁都没说话。

1323
01:01:01.790 --> 01:01:03.050
Just an aerosol can.
只有喷雾罐的声音。

1324
01:01:03.630 --> 01:01:05.470
Longer than you have to stay on a bull.
比骑牛比赛要求的坚持时间还长。

1325
01:01:06.370 --> 01:01:07.190
That's true.
确实。

1326
01:01:07.190 --> 01:01:11.510
Thank you for bringing my measurement of time back to bull riding.
谢谢你又把我的时间衡量标准拉回到了骑牛比赛上。

1327
01:01:13.130 --> 01:01:19.530
Well, also, I don't know if you noticed in this scene, I kept my gaze on the camera.
还有，不知道你有没有注意到，在这场戏里，我的视线一直盯着摄像机。

1328
01:01:19.670 --> 01:01:22.150
I never looked up to Steve.
我一次都没抬头看史蒂夫。

1329
01:01:22.370 --> 01:01:24.090
And I did this for two reasons.
我这么做有两个原因。

1330
01:01:24.090 --> 01:01:28.770
One, because it just felt like I'm in charge of operating the camera.
第一，因为这让我感觉自己真的在负责操作摄像机。

1331
01:01:28.770 --> 01:01:32.290
And so I was going to make sure he stayed in frame.
我要确保他一直保持在取景框里。

1332
01:01:32.430 --> 01:01:34.190
And that just seemed like sort of my job.
这似乎就是我的工作。

1333
01:01:34.350 --> 01:01:39.150
But the other reason was because I could look at the little plastic corner.
但另一个原因是，我可以盯着那个塑料小角落看。

1334
01:01:39.630 --> 01:01:42.790
And then I wouldn't have to actually see Steve.
这样我就不用真的去面对史蒂夫了。

1335
01:01:43.070 --> 01:01:45.130
And it was easier for me not to laugh.
这样我也更容易忍住不笑。

1336
01:01:45.650 --> 01:01:46.990
I wondered about that.
我之前就在想这个问题。

1337
01:01:47.150 --> 01:01:50.130
I was like, A, it looks like you're really operating a video camera.
我在想，首先，你看上去真的很像在操作摄像机。

1338
01:01:50.270 --> 01:01:53.430
But how lucky were you that you didn't have to make eye contact?
但你多幸运啊，不用和他进行眼神交流。

1339
01:01:53.650 --> 01:01:54.810
Because you would have burst into laughter.
因为你肯定会笑喷的。

1340
01:01:55.250 --> 01:02:01.170
Also, when rain drops one of the cue cards and it makes a thud on the ground, that made me laugh.
还有，当雷恩掉了一张提示卡，发出“砰”的一声落地时，那段把我逗乐了。

1341
01:02:02.790 --> 01:02:07.670
It was like, when I was re-watching the scene, I was breaking constantly.
重看那场戏的时候，我简直一直在笑场。

1342
01:02:07.870 --> 01:02:08.650
Those poor guys.
那几个可怜的家伙。

1343
01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:12.430
I mean, they must have been like, Jenna, you need to leave the room.
我想他们当时肯定在想：“珍娜，你得离开这个房间。”

1344
01:02:12.990 --> 01:02:19.290
Well, there is a deleted scene of, you know, Michael does the first video and he's not happy with it, right?
其实有个删减片段，你知道的，迈克尔拍了第一个视频，但他不满意，对吧？

1345
01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:23.710
Well, in the deleted scenes, Jenna, there is his second take at the video.
珍娜，在删减片段里，有他拍的第二个版本。

1346
01:02:23.910 --> 01:02:25.390
You know, you guys shoot the first one.
你们拍了第一个版本。

1347
01:02:25.590 --> 01:02:26.830
Yeah, and he doesn't like it.
对，他不满意。

1348
01:02:26.990 --> 01:02:28.190
He doesn't like it.
他不喜欢。

1349
01:02:28.190 --> 01:02:30.370
And there is a deleted scene.
而且还有一个删减片段。

1350
01:02:30.770 --> 01:02:33.190
And Jenna, it made me laugh so hard.
珍娜，那段真的把我笑坏了。

1351
01:02:33.830 --> 01:02:36.790
Michael goes on to say, I need this job.
迈克尔接着说，我需要这份工作。

1352
01:02:36.950 --> 01:02:39.090
My mortgage is hundreds of dollars a month.
我的房贷每个月要好几百美元。

1353
01:02:39.330 --> 01:02:41.330
With this job, I can barely cover that.
有了这份工作，我才勉强能付得起。

1354
01:02:41.470 --> 01:02:43.990
I have a company car, but I still have to pay for the gas.
我有公司配车，但我还得自己付油钱。

1355
01:02:44.110 --> 01:02:45.170
Gas prices are high.
油价太高了。

1356
01:02:45.290 --> 01:02:47.210
And I have no savings whatsoever.
而且我一点存款都没有。

1357
01:02:48.330 --> 01:02:49.190
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1358
01:02:49.710 --> 01:02:53.670
What's kind of fun for this, for those folks who like to catch things in the background,
对于那些喜欢捕捉背景细节的观众来说，这挺有意思的，

1359
01:02:53.730 --> 01:02:56.850
is that deleted scene dialogue is on the cue card.
因为被删减的台词就在提词卡上。

1360
01:02:56.850 --> 01:02:59.030
And their second attempt is right there.
他们的第二次尝试就在那儿。

1361
01:02:59.170 --> 01:03:00.290
You can zoom in and see it.
你可以放大画面看一看。

1362
01:03:00.770 --> 01:03:05.730
Yeah, a lot of people wrote in to ask, how come what Michael is saying isn't what is printed
是啊，很多人写信来问，为什么迈克尔说的话和提词卡上印的，

1363
01:03:05.730 --> 01:03:07.910
on the cue cards when they go back and forth?
在他们来回切换时不一样？

1364
01:03:08.150 --> 01:03:10.190
It was just because we cut some stuff out.
那是因为我们剪掉了一些内容。

1365
01:03:10.310 --> 01:03:11.890
We trimmed out some stuff.
我们删减了一些片段。

1366
01:03:12.450 --> 01:03:14.730
Yeah, he actually said everything that was on the cards.
没错，他其实把卡片上的内容全说了。

1367
01:03:14.730 --> 01:03:16.610
We just had to lose some of it for time.
只是为了控制时长，我们不得不删掉一些。

1368
01:03:16.610 --> 01:03:21.490
Well, over in accounting, we had someone write in.
好，会计部那边，有人写信来了。

1369
01:03:22.610 --> 01:03:27.530
Megan Allman said, 17 minutes, six seconds, Kevin sass.
梅根·奥尔曼说，17分06秒，凯文的毒舌。

1370
01:03:28.530 --> 01:03:31.410
Yeah, serious Kevin sass.
没错，非常严肃的凯文式毒舌。

1371
01:03:31.550 --> 01:03:34.410
Like he's been holding it in for so long.
就像他憋了很久一样。

1372
01:03:34.410 --> 01:03:35.870
He just couldn't wait.
他简直等不及了。

1373
01:03:36.010 --> 01:03:37.610
Now he's got something on her.
现在他抓住了她的把柄。

1374
01:03:37.610 --> 01:03:41.490
Yeah, Angela is critiquing Kevin's math skills.
是啊，安吉拉在批评凯文的数学能力。

1375
01:03:42.390 --> 01:03:48.790
And he then gives some sass by insulting your customer relations skills.
然后他反唇相讥，嘲讽了你的客户关系处理能力。

1376
01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:50.490
Yeah.
没错。

1377
01:03:50.750 --> 01:03:52.090
And then I call them apes.
然后我叫他们猿猴。

1378
01:03:52.230 --> 01:03:53.830
And then Oscar's like, apologize for that.
接着奥斯卡就说，为那个道歉。

1379
01:03:53.890 --> 01:03:54.830
And I'm like, oh, I'm sorry.
我就说，噢，抱歉。

1380
01:03:54.830 --> 01:03:56.010
You're both morons.
你们俩都是白痴。

1381
01:03:56.510 --> 01:03:58.230
And they're like, but you said sorry.
他们就说，但你刚才道歉了。

1382
01:03:58.430 --> 01:04:02.570
It's like I'm sitting with my two junior high brothers.
感觉就像在和我的两个初中生弟弟坐在一起。

1383
01:04:02.870 --> 01:04:03.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1384
01:04:03.230 --> 01:04:04.190
That's what they're like.
他们就是那样。

1385
01:04:04.190 --> 01:04:09.530
And I want you to know that Brian and Oscar improvised their sort of little high five at
我想让你们知道，布莱恩和奥斯卡最后那个击掌是即兴发挥的，

1386
01:04:09.530 --> 01:04:12.130
the end and that they don't quite get it right.
而且他们没完全对上。

1387
01:04:12.350 --> 01:04:14.770
They were so tickled by that moment.
他们被那个瞬间逗乐了。

1388
01:04:15.150 --> 01:04:17.670
They kept cracking up.
他们一直在笑场。

1389
01:04:17.870 --> 01:04:19.330
Brian kept cracking up.
布莱恩一直在笑场。

1390
01:04:19.510 --> 01:04:20.410
I love that.
我喜欢那个瞬间。

1391
01:04:20.890 --> 01:04:23.450
And they like did a few different tries at it.
他们试了好几种不同的拍法。

1392
01:04:23.530 --> 01:04:25.950
And it just was like their favorite thing.
那简直成了他们最喜欢的部分。

1393
01:04:26.490 --> 01:04:28.430
OK, well, I loved that moment.
好的，我非常喜欢那个瞬间。

1394
01:04:28.450 --> 01:04:29.790
It made me laugh.
它把我逗笑了。

1395
01:04:30.130 --> 01:04:30.810
Me too.
我也是。

1396
01:04:30.810 --> 01:04:34.050
Because why couldn't they have just high five?
因为他们为什么就不能好好击个掌呢？

1397
01:04:34.310 --> 01:04:39.670
They were kind of doing like a coronavirus high five where you don't actually touch.
他们当时做的就像是新冠时期的那种不接触击掌。

1398
01:04:39.810 --> 01:04:42.230
Well, and they were trying to do like a fist bump and air.
嗯，他们当时想做的是那种隔空碰拳。

1399
01:04:42.410 --> 01:04:43.450
And but they're right there.
但他们明明离得那么近。

1400
01:04:43.590 --> 01:04:45.430
They could have easily touched one another.
他们完全可以轻松地碰到对方。

1401
01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:46.850
But that's what it made me think of.
但这让我联想到了那个。

1402
01:04:46.990 --> 01:04:49.050
I think they love the Jim Pam air high five.
我觉得他们很喜欢吉姆和帕姆那种空中击掌。

1403
01:04:49.250 --> 01:04:50.790
This is their dude version.
这是他们的兄弟版。

1404
01:04:52.110 --> 01:04:56.350
Also, it would have meant that one of them would have would had to get up or lean over
而且，这意味着他们其中一人必须站起来或者探过身去，

1405
01:04:56.350 --> 01:04:57.210
awkwardly.
姿势会很尴尬。

1406
01:04:57.470 --> 01:05:03.250
And so I just they were like, oh, OK, well, I guess it was an optical illusion because
所以他们当时就觉得，哦，好吧，我猜那是个视觉错觉，因为

1407
01:05:03.250 --> 01:05:06.930
it seemed like maybe they could have just made a connection.
看起来他们好像本可以击掌成功的。

1408
01:05:07.290 --> 01:05:09.210
It would have required one of them getting up.
但这需要其中一人站起来才行。

1409
01:05:09.350 --> 01:05:09.810
And I see.
我明白了。

1410
01:05:10.050 --> 01:05:11.690
OK, well, there you go for it.
好吧，原来是这样。

1411
01:05:12.530 --> 01:05:17.510
Well, maybe we should go back to the high school for a second because we forgot to mention
嗯，也许我们应该回到高中那段聊聊，因为我们忘了提

1412
01:05:17.510 --> 01:05:27.520
that Andy and Jim do meet with the principal and it doesn't really go well because Andy
安迪和吉姆确实见了校长，但过程并不顺利，因为安迪

1413
01:05:27.520 --> 01:05:31.740
is so preoccupied by learning that his girlfriend is at the high school.
满脑子都在想他女朋友就在那所高中里。

1414
01:05:32.640 --> 01:05:33.920
Yeah, I don't really know.
是啊，我也不太清楚。

1415
01:05:34.060 --> 01:05:35.180
Did they get this account back?
他们把那个客户拿回来了吗？

1416
01:05:35.180 --> 01:05:36.040
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1417
01:05:36.220 --> 01:05:39.500
It just seems like Andy's about to have a breakdown and Jim is just trying to get them
看起来安迪快要崩溃了，而吉姆只是想带他们

1418
01:05:39.500 --> 01:05:39.940
out of there.
离开那里。

1419
01:05:40.280 --> 01:05:45.940
Well, the principal was played by Jim Jansen, who also played Reverend Skinner on Gilmore
嗯，校长是由吉姆·詹森饰演的，他还在《吉尔莫女孩》里演过斯金纳牧师。

1420
01:05:45.940 --> 01:05:46.300
Girls.
一点小花絮。

1421
01:05:46.680 --> 01:05:47.500
A little bit of trivia.
哦，这花絮真不错。

1422
01:05:47.500 --> 01:05:49.460
Oh, that is good trivia.
我知道。

1423
01:05:49.780 --> 01:05:50.060
I know.
是啊，我们确实没看到后续如何。

1424
01:05:50.340 --> 01:05:53.400
And yeah, we don't really find out how that went.
但在开车回家的路上，安迪显然还是很沮丧，吉姆想

1425
01:05:54.140 --> 01:05:59.920
But as they're driving home in the car, Andy is still clearly bummed out and Jim wants
让他振作起来。

1426
01:05:59.920 --> 01:06:01.000
to cheer him up.
我是说，吉姆在这里真的是拼了。

1427
01:06:01.540 --> 01:06:04.140
I mean, Jim really, really goes for it here.
他开始唱，哦，威莫，哦，威莫，哦，威莫，哦，威莫。

1428
01:06:04.300 --> 01:06:09.380
He just starts going, oh, we moe, oh, we moe, oh, we moe, oh, we moe.
是啊。

1429
01:06:09.440 --> 01:06:09.580
Yeah.
安迪还在抵抗。

1430
01:06:09.840 --> 01:06:11.040
And Andy's fighting it.
他在抵抗。

1431
01:06:11.140 --> 01:06:11.840
He's fighting it.
但最后他还是忍不住了。

1432
01:06:11.960 --> 01:06:13.440
But then he just he can't resiSt.
他就像是，哦，他忍不住了。

1433
01:06:13.660 --> 01:06:17.080
He's like, oh, he can't.
没法不加入进去。

1434
01:06:17.080 --> 01:06:18.260
Not jump in.
你还记得剧里有次我们在办公区一起唱这首歌吗？

1435
01:06:19.360 --> 01:06:25.140
Do you remember that time on the show when we all sang that in the bullpen?
那是为了拍戏还是我们那天随口唱的？

1436
01:06:25.400 --> 01:06:28.660
Was that for an episode or were we just doing that one day?
我觉得是我们随口就开始唱了。

1437
01:06:29.080 --> 01:06:31.040
I think we just started doing it.
是啊。

1438
01:06:31.340 --> 01:06:31.800
Yeah.
因为一旦有人起头，这歌确实挺有感染力的。

1439
01:06:31.920 --> 01:06:35.120
Because it is kind of infectious when someone starts it.
是啊。

1440
01:06:35.240 --> 01:06:35.460
Yeah.
我们当时有点神志不清了。

1441
01:06:35.580 --> 01:06:37.040
We were just a little loopy.
我也这么觉得。

1442
01:06:37.040 --> 01:06:37.960
I think so, too.
在丛林里，那寂静的。

1443
01:06:41.150 --> 01:06:43.310
In the jungle, the quiet.
是啊。

1444
01:06:43.690 --> 01:06:44.210
Yeah.
哦，在结束本集进入那个精彩的片尾彩蛋前，还有最后一件事，关于克里德。

1445
01:06:44.470 --> 01:06:51.450
Oh, one last thing now before we end this episode and get to this amazing tag is Creed.
是啊。

1446
01:06:52.330 --> 01:06:52.850
Yeah.
克里德害那个女人被解雇了。

1447
01:06:53.670 --> 01:06:55.310
Creed got this woman fired.
然后他还在办公室里到处为她募捐。

1448
01:06:55.730 --> 01:06:58.450
And he's going around the office collecting money for her.
他打算把钱放进贺卡里。

1449
01:06:58.590 --> 01:06:59.950
He's going to put it in a card.
你懂的。

1450
01:07:00.350 --> 01:07:01.090
You know.
你懂的。

1451
01:07:01.090 --> 01:07:05.130
So, why do bad things always happen to good people, he asks.
所以，他问，为什么坏事总是发生在好人身上。

1452
01:07:05.570 --> 01:07:07.350
And then he tosses the card.
然后他把卡片扔了。

1453
01:07:07.350 --> 01:07:08.870
He puts the money in his pocket.
他把钱放进了口袋。

1454
01:07:09.130 --> 01:07:10.510
Creed is diabolical.
克里德真是太邪恶了。

1455
01:07:10.990 --> 01:07:11.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1456
01:07:12.350 --> 01:07:17.610
And we also find out that, in Pam's opinion, Michael made the best apology video ever.
我们还发现，在帕姆看来，迈克尔拍出了史上最棒的道歉视频。

1457
01:07:17.790 --> 01:07:18.230
Yeah.
没错。

1458
01:07:18.350 --> 01:07:20.250
That ended with an ultimatum.
那个视频最后还下了最后通牒。

1459
01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:21.330
You have one day.
你们只有一天时间。

1460
01:07:21.510 --> 01:07:21.790
What?
什么？

1461
01:07:22.310 --> 01:07:22.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1462
01:07:23.210 --> 01:07:24.950
And where are these videos going, Jenna?
那么这些视频最后都去哪了呢，珍娜？

1463
01:07:25.250 --> 01:07:26.090
Where is that going?
那东西最后去哪了？

1464
01:07:31.090 --> 01:07:31.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1465
01:07:31.710 --> 01:07:34.250
Well, now we have such a fun tag.
好吧，现在我们有一个很有趣的尾声。

1466
01:07:34.430 --> 01:07:37.170
And Rain had so much fun doing this.
雷恩拍这段的时候玩得很开心。

1467
01:07:37.550 --> 01:07:37.770
Yes.
是的。

1468
01:07:38.270 --> 01:07:42.410
Dwight arrives for work the next day dressed as Jim.
第二天德怀特打扮成吉姆的样子来上班。

1469
01:07:43.470 --> 01:07:47.790
But it backfires a little bit because everybody just compliments him on how great he looks.
但结果适得其反，因为大家都在夸他看起来棒极了。

1470
01:07:47.970 --> 01:07:49.130
And he gets a little frustrated.
他感到有点沮丧。

1471
01:07:49.970 --> 01:07:53.010
And he tries to do, like, the Jim look to camera.
他还试着模仿吉姆对着镜头做表情。

1472
01:07:53.170 --> 01:07:53.430
Yes.
没错。

1473
01:07:53.550 --> 01:07:54.970
But it's, like, so awkward.
但看起来太尴尬了。

1474
01:07:56.210 --> 01:07:56.730
Yes.
确实。

1475
01:07:56.730 --> 01:08:03.690
Well, I want to tell you that this was originally in the script as the alternate ending to the cold open.
我想告诉你们，这段戏最初在剧本里是作为开场戏的备选结尾。

1476
01:08:04.210 --> 01:08:10.250
Dwight had a little talking head where he said, to defeat your enemy, you have to become your enemy.
德怀特原本有个采访片段，他说，要打败你的敌人，你必须成为你的敌人。

1477
01:08:11.070 --> 01:08:13.210
And then he showed up to work dressed as Jim.
然后他才打扮成吉姆的样子来上班。

1478
01:08:13.350 --> 01:08:15.870
But in the editing process, we split it up.
但在剪辑过程中，我们把它分开了。

1479
01:08:16.170 --> 01:08:17.910
Which I think was genius.
我觉得这真是天才之举。

1480
01:08:18.390 --> 01:08:19.430
I love that.
我喜欢这个安排。

1481
01:08:19.610 --> 01:08:20.850
I love that we end with it.
我喜欢把它作为结尾。

1482
01:08:20.850 --> 01:08:23.910
I remember how much fun Rain had doing this scene.
我记得雷恩拍这场戏时玩得有多开心。

1483
01:08:24.070 --> 01:08:33.610
But I also remember him talking with Randall, the director, about how Dwight couldn't be as good of a mimic as Jim.
但我也记得他和导演兰德尔讨论过，德怀特不可能像吉姆那样擅长模仿。

1484
01:08:34.110 --> 01:08:44.110
So whereas Jim could come in and just do this spot-on impression, they sort of felt like Dwight's version of Jim had to be a little messier.
所以，吉姆可以走进来就模仿得惟妙惟肖，但他们觉得德怀特版的吉姆应该更笨拙一点。

1485
01:08:44.250 --> 01:08:45.950
But, like, how do you thread that needle, right?
但是，这其中的分寸该怎么拿捏呢？

1486
01:08:45.950 --> 01:08:49.910
Like, how do you do an impression, but it's Dwight doing the impression.
就是说，你该怎么去模仿，但又要表现出这是德怀特在模仿。

1487
01:08:50.070 --> 01:08:54.470
Because Rain could do an amazing impression of Jim Halpert.
因为雷恩其实能把吉姆·哈珀特模仿得非常像。

1488
01:08:54.770 --> 01:08:56.730
But he had to do it as Dwight.
但他必须以德怀特的身份去模仿。

1489
01:08:56.850 --> 01:09:00.630
So I remember them playing with that a lot on the set when they were shooting this.
所以我记得他们在片场拍摄时，为了这个反复琢磨了很久。

1490
01:09:01.610 --> 01:09:01.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1491
01:09:01.990 --> 01:09:08.290
I feel like those moments would come up for us where it was, like, your character steps out of its comfort zone a little bit to do something.
我觉得我们经常会遇到这种情况，就是你的角色稍微走出舒适区去做某件事。

1492
01:09:08.410 --> 01:09:11.210
But you still have to do it as your character and through that filter.
但你仍然必须以你角色的身份，通过那个角色的视角去完成。

1493
01:09:11.530 --> 01:09:11.870
Yeah.
没错。

1494
01:09:12.710 --> 01:09:13.910
But it was fun.
但这很有趣。

1495
01:09:13.910 --> 01:09:17.370
It was fun for us to watch those fellas do that.
看着那几个家伙演这些戏对我们来说很有趣。

1496
01:09:17.610 --> 01:09:20.090
Well, you guys, that was Product Recall.
好了，各位，这就是《产品召回》这一集。

1497
01:09:20.270 --> 01:09:22.070
Thanks for taking that journey with us.
感谢你们与我们一同回顾。

1498
01:09:22.190 --> 01:09:26.650
We got off topic a few times, but, you know, there's some real nuggets in this.
我们中间跑题了几次，但你知道，这里面还是有些干货的。

1499
01:09:26.930 --> 01:09:28.730
Lord, bear me strength.
上帝啊，赐予我力量吧。

1500
01:09:29.050 --> 01:09:30.110
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

1501
01:09:30.290 --> 01:09:33.170
And listen, identity theft is not a joke.
听着，身份盗窃可不是闹着玩的。

1502
01:09:33.630 --> 01:09:35.370
Millions of families suffer every year.
每年有数百万个家庭深受其害。

1503
01:09:35.550 --> 01:09:36.130
All right, guys.
好了，各位。

1504
01:09:36.330 --> 01:09:37.650
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1505
01:09:37.750 --> 01:09:38.950
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1506
01:09:39.970 --> 01:09:41.430
Someone bear me a snack.
谁能给我拿点零食。

1507
01:09:41.430 --> 01:09:42.150
I'm hungry.
我饿了。

1508
01:09:42.150 --> 01:09:48.060
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士的第二杯酒》。

